  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIR Swedish Workplace HIV and AIDS Programme SWHAP2014-2018 - NIR Swedish Workplace HIV and AIDS Programme SWHAP</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">NIR Swedish Workplace HIV and AIDS Programme SWHAP2014-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Swedish Workplace HIV and AIDS Programme (SWHAP) bygger p&#xe5; samarbete  med svenska f&#xf6;retag verksamma i Afrika s&#xf6;der om Sahara f&#xf6;r att inf&#xf6;ra h&#xe4;lsof&#xf6;rebyggande program med syfte att f&#xf6;rebygga ytterligare         spridning av HIV p&#xe5; arbetsplatserna. I denna tredje fas av programmet &#xe4;r avsikten att (i) etablera h&#xe5;llbara h&#xe4;lsoprogram p&#xe5; arbetsplatserna som f&#xf6;rbygger HIV, oh&#xe4;lsa och oj&#xe4;mlikhet mellan k&#xf6;nen; (ii) organiser</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Workplace HIV and AIDS Programme (SWHAP) builds on the    network of Swedish companies in Sub-Saharan Africa (SSA) in           introducing wellness programmes with the aim to prevent the further   spread of HIV in the workplace. In this third phase of the programme, the overall outcomes at the end of the project are expected to be;    (i) sustainable workplace programmes responding to HIV, Health and ge</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of SWHAP was to support the establishment and spread of innovative, effective and sustainable HIV/AIDS and Wellness programmes and help to maximise productivity and improve the health and quality of the life of employees, families and surrounding communities.
In order to achieve this, there are three medium-term outcomes:
Outcome 1: Sustainable HIV&amp;AIDS and wellness workplace programmes have been established and enhanced in targeted countries.
Outcome 2: SWHAP initiatives have expanded to secondary beneficiaries beyond the workplaces.
Outcome 3: The SWHAP approach has been made viable and sustainable through its added value to stakeholders and partners.</narrative>
  </description>
